nit: Agno uses `run_response.session_id` over the `session_id` argument when both are passed, so the conversation id can differ from the session that's actually continued.

```suggestion
    if is_continue:
        run_response = get_argument("run_response", wrapped, args, kwargs)
        if run_response is not None:
            sid = getattr(run_response, "session_id", None)
            if sid is not None:
                return str(sid)
    session_id = get_argument("session_id", wrapped, args, kwargs)
    if session_id is not None:
        return str(session_id)
```

`Team.continue_run` accepts serialized requirement dicts ([`requirements: Optional[List[Any]]`](https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/blob/v3.1.6/libs/agno/agno/team/team.py#L1119-L1124), [normalized via `RunRequirement.from_dict`](https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/blob/v3.1.6/libs/agno/agno/team/_run.py#L5697-L5710)). For such a dict `getattr(item, "tool_execution")` is `None`, so this records the requirement's own [`id`](https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/blob/v3.1.6/libs/agno/agno/run/requirement.py#L203-L208) (a random uuid) as the tool call id, with `response=None`. Reusing Agno's parser also picks up top-level `confirmation` / `external_execution_result` ([here](https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/blob/v3.1.6/libs/agno/agno/run/requirement.py#L275-L287)):

```suggestion
        if isinstance(item, Mapping):
            from agno.run.requirement import RunRequirement

            item = RunRequirement.from_dict(
                cast(dict[str, Any], item)
            ).tool_execution

        # Agno populates tool_call_id on paused tools; without an ID the result
        # cannot be correlated to a prior tool call.
        if isinstance(item, ToolExecution) and item.tool_call_id:
            tool_executions.append(item)
```

Regression test (fails today with `{'id': 'req-uuid', 'response': None}`):

```python
def test_team_continue_run_dict_requirement(
    instrument_agno_content_capture, span_exporter
) -> None:
    from agno.team import Team

    req = {
        "id": "req-uuid",
        "tool_execution": {
            "tool_call_id": "call_1",
            "tool_name": "lookup",
            "tool_args": {},
        },
        "external_execution_result": "Delivered",
    }
    team = Team(name="t", members=[], model=MockModel(id="mock-model"))
    with patch(
        "agno.team._run.continue_run_dispatch",
        return_value=ModelResponse(content="ok"),
    ):
        team.continue_run(run_id="r", session_id="s", requirements=[req])

    span = span_exporter.get_finished_spans()[-1]
    messages = json.loads(span.attributes[GenAIAttributes.GEN_AI_INPUT_MESSAGES])
    assert messages[0]["parts"] == [
        {"type": "tool_call_response", "id": "call_1", "response": "Delivered"}
    ]
```
